prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of the nurses' office of a hospital ward in the early afternoon, empty for a moment just before the shift change, taken by a nurse standing in the doorway, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus from the floor in the foreground to the back wall. Natural colours, white ceiling light and soft daylight from a window on the right. The textures of real steel, plastic, glass, paper, cardboard and wood, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

The reference photograph is a real phone photograph taken in a hospital of the same city. Use it for the photographic look only: the same true-to-life phone-camera rendering, the same natural colours and soft daylight, the same fine detail and real textures, nothing drawn, painted or rendered. Its room, its furniture and its person do not appear here; this is a different place.

Every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. The whole room carries no writing, numbers, print, symbol or logo anywhere: every paper is blank or carries only grey lines and empty boxes, every screen shows only plain coloured panels, the boxes and bottles are plain white with no labels, the wall clock has a plain white face with only twelve short black tick marks, and the room looks as it could look in any modern hospital in Europe or America.

THE BACK WALL, from left to right:
- a large white magnetic board on the wall, ruled into a plain grid of empty grey boxes, with a few round magnets in red, green and blue stuck on it; it carries no writing;
- beside it, a printed sheet pinned to a small cork board: a large plain grid of small coloured squares in pale yellow, pale blue and pale green, like a monthly rota, with no letters or numbers;
- above them, a round wall clock with a plain white face and twelve short black tick marks;
- to the right, a tall white medicine cupboard with two glass doors, its shelves full of plain white boxes of different sizes;
- beside the tall cupboard, a small grey steel wall cabinet with a single closed door and a round silver lock, mounted at head height.

THE LONG DESK runs along the left-hand wall, a white worktop seen from slightly to the side. On it, from the back to the front of the picture:
- a computer screen showing plain pale-blue and white panels with grey bars, and a keyboard and a mouse in front of it;
- a black desk telephone with its handset in place;
- a small white printer with a blank sheet of paper in its tray;
- a brown clipboard holding a blank sheet ruled with grey lines;
- a loose sheet of paper ruled into an empty table, lying flat;
- a white mug of coffee, half full;
- a grey blood pressure monitor with its folded grey arm cuff;
- a small white blood sugar meter beside a small round box of test strips;
- a white digital ear thermometer lying in its holder.
A grey office chair on castors stands pushed under the desk.

THE MIDDLE OF THE ROOM, on the pale grey floor:
- a white medicine trolley on castors with four shallow drawers; on its top, a row of small plastic pill organisers with clear lids divided into four compartments each, some holding small white and yellow tablets;
- beside it, a box of blue disposable gloves with one glove pulled half out of the opening, and a small yellow plastic sharps bin with a closed lid, both standing on the top of the trolley at its far end.

THE RIGHT OF THE PICTURE:
- a small white refrigerator under the window, waist high, with a plain white door;
- in the front right corner, a red emergency trolley on castors with five drawers, and standing on its top a compact grey defibrillator with a dark screen and a carrying handle;
- on the right-hand wall by the door, at shoulder height, a plain white hand-disinfectant dispenser with a short steel lever;
- the window above the refrigerator shows a pale sky and the green crowns of trees.

The floor is pale grey vinyl, the walls are warm white, and the bottom of the picture shows the floor in front of the medicine trolley. The room is tidy, bright and calm, as if the nurses had just stepped out.
